{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && grep -rn \\\"ReloadConfig\\\" --include=*.go . | grep -v _test | head; echo ===; grep -n \\\"func (r \\\\*Raft) ReloadConfig\\\" -A 50 api.go\"","aggregated_output":"./config.go:185:\t// This can be tuned during operation using ReloadConfig.\n./config.go:192:\t// ReloadConfig.\n./config.go:198:\t// setting used. This can be tuned during operation using ReloadConfig.\n./config.go:276:// runtime using raft.ReloadConfig. We choose to duplicate fields over embedding\n./api.go:761:// ReloadConfig updates the configuration of a running raft node. If the new\n./api.go:765:func (r *Raft) ReloadConfig(rc ReloadableConfig) error {\n===\n765:func (r *Raft) ReloadConfig(rc ReloadableConfig) error {\n766-\tr.confReloadMu.Lock()\n767-\tdefer r.confReloadMu.Unlock()\n768-\n769-\t// Load the current config (note we are under a lock so it can't be changed\n770-\t// between this read and a later Store).\n771-\toldCfg := r.config()\n772-\n773-\t// Set the reloadable fields\n774-\tnewCfg := rc.apply(oldCfg)\n775-\n776-\tif err := ValidateConfig(&newCfg); err != nil {\n777-\t\treturn err\n778-\t}\n779-\tr.conf.Store(newCfg)\n780-\n781-\tif rc.HeartbeatTimeout < oldCfg.HeartbeatTimeout {\n782-\t\t// On leader, ensure replication loops running with a longer\n783-\t\t// timeout than what we want now discover the change.\n784-\t\tasyncNotifyCh(r.leaderNotifyCh)\n785-\t\t// On follower, update current timer to use the shorter new value.\n786-\t\tasyncNotifyCh(r.followerNotifyCh)\n787-\t}\n788-\treturn nil\n789-}\n790-\n791-// ReloadableConfig returns the current state of the reloadable fields in Raft's\n792-// configuration. This is useful for programs to discover the current state for\n793-// reporting to users or tests. It is safe to call from any goroutine. It is\n794-// intended for reporting and testing purposes primarily; external\n795-// synchronization would be required to safely use this in a read-modify-write\n796-// pattern for reloadable configuration options.\n797-func (r *Raft) ReloadableConfig() ReloadableConfig {\n798-\tcfg := r.config()\n799-\tvar rc ReloadableConfig\n800-\trc.fromConfig(cfg)\n801-\treturn rc\n802-}\n803-\n804-// BootstrapCluster is equivalent to non-member BootstrapCluster but can be\n805-// called on an un-bootstrapped Raft instance after it has been created. This\n806-// should only be called at the beginning of time for the cluster with an\n807-// identical configuration listing all Voter servers. There is no need to\n808-// bootstrap Nonvoter and Staging servers.\n809-//\n810-// A cluster can only be bootstrapped once from a single participating Voter\n811-// server. Any further attempts to bootstrap will return an error that can be\n812-// safely ignored.\n813-//\n814-// One sane approach is to bootstrap a single server with a configuration\n815-// listing just itself as a Voter, then invoke AddVoter() on it to add other\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
